course: dictionary
lesson: 11589
title: Antique: old and worth keeping
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An antique is something very old that people value because it is old, rare or beautiful. «Grandma bought an antique clock at the market.» The clue is that it is old, and people want it because of that. Antique can be a noun (an antique) or an adjective that describes a thing (antique furniture).
explain: Look at the words around it. «The shop sells antique furniture and old maps.» Furniture is something for the home, and the word antique tells you it is old and valuable. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The shop sells old, valuable furniture and old maps" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Be careful, because people sometimes use antique as a joke. «My brother's phone is an antique, it only has buttons!» Here it does not mean a hundred years old. It means very old-fashioned. Read the whole sentence to see which meaning the writer chose.
fact: An antique is usually a hundred years old or more.
fact: As a noun, antique means an old object: «The antique was sold for a lot of money.»
fact: As an adjective, antique describes something old and valuable: «antique furniture» or «an antique vase».
fact: An antique dealer buys and sells antiques, and an antique shop is where they are sold.
fact: Used as a joke, antique can mean very old-fashioned, like a slow old computer.
exercise: «The shop sold antique furniture and old maps.» What does antique mean in this sentence? | Small and light | Brand new and cheap | Broken and useless | *Old and valuable
exercise: «Grandma's antique clock has ticked for over a hundred years.» Which word tells you the clock is old? | clock | *hundred | ticked | Grandma's
exercise: Tom says, «My old laptop is an antique, it only plays CDs!» What does antique mean here? | Worth a lot of money | *Very old-fashioned, said as a joke | Made of solid gold | Found in a museum
test: In «She bought an antique at the fair», what is an antique? | A kind of computer | A type of shop | A brand-new toy | *An old object valued because it is old, rare or beautiful
test: «Dad's antique watch was found in a dusty box in the attic.» What does antique mean? | New and shiny | *Old and valuable | Funny | Broken and useless
exam: Mia's great-grandmother's antique necklace is priceless. What does antique mean here? | A type of cloth | Lost and found | Shiny and new | *Old and valuable
